# cursor: its API, where its login polls too (api2), its agent's hosts, which api2's server config
# names (agent.api5 and its regional hosts, which its package doesn't name, so all of them), and its
# codebase indexing (repo42). Its metrics host (api3), its updates (downloads.cursor.com) and Sentry are
# left out: blocking them costs nothing, and its updates are off.
api2.cursor.sh
api5.cursor.sh
*.api5.cursor.sh
repo42.cursor.sh
# The host Cursor documents for Tab requests; Cursor's CLI uses it for its metrics, its
# MetricsService's reports, fire and forget (the metricsUrl in the 2026.11.11 package's
# service-urls, read, not run): https://cursor.com/docs/enterprise/network-configuration
quiet api3.cursor.sh
